Arraylists:
1.  An arraylist uses an array datastructure to store values.
2.  Arraylists are good for random access using index.
3.  First item is 0th item.
4.  Vectors are synchronized and array lists are not synchronized.
5.  Except accessing all other operations on arrays take O(n) time,
    Like deletion, arraylists are not good for deletion, we should use linked lists for that.
6.  We can define capicity of an arraylist at the time of creation ArrayList(10000);, this will
    save array list to expand and copy items every time because inital size will be 10000 values.
7.  Data in arraylist is stored consecutively.
8.  Deleting items from front and mid of large arraylist can cause performance degradation.